          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Pandiyan and Kumudha are asleep from exhaustion. Paranthaman comes, fires, and runs away; the shot hits the large mirror. Pandiyan and Kumudha wake and cling to each other in fear.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u002",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Paranthaman runs down the stairs. Hearing the sound, Poomalai comes crying 'Kumudha, Kumudha' and meets him on the staircase.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u003",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d001",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "Paranthaman! You sinner! What have you done!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u004",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d002",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "Leave me. In this world Paranthaman must have neither enemies nor people who are of no use to him!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u005",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "(He says this and leaves in fury.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u006",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d003",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "Kumudha! Kumudha!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u007",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "(She runs upstairs.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u008",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Kumudha's room.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u009",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d004",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Screaming) Kumudha...",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u010",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d005",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chinnamma... (embracing her)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u011",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d006",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "Someone has tried to kill me.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u012",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d007",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 61,
            "printedPage": 53
          }
        ],
        "text": "Who else could it be? It is the enemy within our own house, Chinnamma! Either we must leave this house, or your brother must leave.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u013",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d008",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "What right do you or I have to tell him to leave?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u014",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d009",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "So you have the right only to let my husband be murdered?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u015",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d010",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "Kumudha! What is this!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u016",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d011",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "Let her speak. Let her speak. She alone was left! Once she too has spoken, what more is left for me?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u017",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d012",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "Pandiyan! Please listen to what I say. You and Kumudha should leave this town for a few days....",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u018",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d013",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "Out of fear of death? Uh-uh...",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u019",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d014",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "For my Kumudha. So that the flower-grove swaying in her hair is not destroyed, grant me this one boon, Pandiyan. My Kumudha has never even touched suffering. I know that even if she were cut into pieces, you are the great medicine that could join them again without breaking continuity. I will not allow that medicine, Kumudha's feast of happiness, to be destroyed. Please. I sacrificed my love for you, did I not? (Kumudha action.) In the name of that sacrifice, in the name of that love, I ask you. I beg you. Agree.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u020",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d015",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chinnamma... (runs to her).",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u021",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d016",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "Look at my Kumudha, Pandiyan. Protect her so that her life is not ruined. Both of you go to Madras. You can return after your enemy's anger has subsided......",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s047-u022",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s047-d017",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 62,
            "printedPage": 54
          }
        ],
        "text": "All right. We will do as you wish......",
        "notes": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
